kfree(map->debugfs_name);
```
Reason:
The unconditional allocation of `debugfs_name` using `kasprintf` without checking if it had already been allocated leads to a memory leak when `regmap_attach_dev` is called. If `debugfs_name` was previously allocated, it is not freed before a new allocation is attempted, resulting in lost memory references. Additionally, the code incorrectly attempts to free `debugfs_name` when it is already NULL, which can cause undefined behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!map->debugfs_name) {
    map->debugfs_name = kasprintf(GFP_KERNEL, "%s-%s", devname, name);
}
if (!map->debugfs_name)
    return;
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a check to ensure that `debugfs_name` is only allocated if it has not already been allocated. This prevents the memory leak by avoiding a new allocation without freeing the previous one. Additionally, the check after the allocation ensures that if the allocation fails, the function exits gracefully, preventing further operations on a NULL pointer.

